letes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"] " / 26 January 1924 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/533"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002493"} "Hermann Kleeberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002467"} "Henning Olsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The 5,000 metres was heavily influenced by the weather. As the race progressed, wind and snow grew stronger, and ice conditions deteriorated. This placed the skaters who had been drawn late in the competition at a disadvantage. The first favorite to hit the ice was " [:a {:href "/athletes/83820"} "Ivar Ballangrud"] ". The 24-year-old Norwegian was the 1926 World Champion, and had won the 5 km race at the World Championships in Davos just a week before. He took great advantage of the weather conditions in his race, skating a steady race and lapping his Lithuanian opponent. His time of 8:50.5 was a far cry from the times skated in Davos, where Ballangrud had approached the World Record (which stood at 8:26.5)."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/85582"} "Bernt Evensen"] " took off faster than Ballangrud, and had the fastest time until two-thirds of the race, when he faded and finished ten seconds behind his countryman. His time was approached by the best American distance skater, " [:a {:href "/athletes/87432"} "Irving Jaffee"] ", of New York. He gained on Evensen every lap, but ended up 0.2 seconds short. The 38-year-old Finnish veteran " [:a {:href "/athletes/97613"} "Julius Skutnabb"] " had a similar build up, but won two seconds on the Norwegian in the final lap, moving into silver medal position."] "\n\n" [:p {} "By then, weather conditions had become really tough. Norwegian " [:a {:href "/athletes/84606"} "Armand Carlsen"] " came within half a second of the bronze medal, and would likely have medaled had it not been for the snow. Other favorites finished further back, including two 5000 metre medalists from the recent World Championships, " [:a {:href "/athletes/97757"} "Michael Staksrud"] " (NOR) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"] " (FIN). Thunberg’s luck was especially bad, considering that he had originally been drawn in the third race. Because his pairmate, the Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/86149"} "Charlie Gorman"] ", didn’t show up, he was moved to the end of the competition to race " [:a {:href "/athletes/98704"} "Arthur Vollstedt"] "."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button853836", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button853836').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "600 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1000 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1400 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1800 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2600 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3000 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3400 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3800 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "4200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "4600 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td 